WEBVTT


00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:07.400
This is my interactive AI agent ecosystem dungeon in space

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.480
that I have all of my AI agents living inside of.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.520
And I organize them in all these different rooms.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.700
For example, we have the two factory rooms

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:19.181
where they're running their own autonomous businesses out of.

00:00:19.182 --> 00:00:20.221
And this conveyor belt

00:00:20.222 --> 00:00:23.161
is a representation of the Etsy store it started

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.020
that it's almost made $2,000 on and everything.

00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:28.301
I don't do any work for this.

00:00:28.302 --> 00:00:32.061
It runs itself. Inside of these two rooms here we have an a.

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:35.541
We have an AI research agent that's constantly doing research,

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:36.101
for example,

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:39.261
on the autonomous businesses that it started and its competitors,

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:42.101
to see what inspiration we could take from the competitors

00:00:42.102 --> 00:00:43.821
and how we can apply it to our own

00:00:43.822 --> 00:00:45.181
autonomous businesses that we build.

00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:49.461
We have a whole bunch of crazy ass shit going on

00:00:49.462 --> 00:00:51.901
in this entire station here.

00:00:51.902 --> 00:00:54.141
And in this video in particular,

00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:56.821
I actually want to focus on this room here,

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:57.941
which is the armoury room.

00:00:57.942 --> 00:01:03.701
And this is where my agent builds and manages its own skills

00:01:03.702 --> 00:01:07.421
on Openclap. And we're gonna open up the terminal here

00:01:07.422 --> 00:01:08.741
and you're gonna see actually

00:01:08.742 --> 00:01:12.021
all of the accounts and API keys I have connected,

00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:14.581
like my YouTube channel, the Etsy store is connected.

00:01:14.582 --> 00:01:15.941
And I could just in one place,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:19.021
see everything that's attached to my AI agents

00:01:19.022 --> 00:01:20.401
and what they have access to.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:25.340
And in the skills tab, we have all of the skills that it Has built

00:01:25.341 --> 00:01:27.661
and rather replicated would be a better word.

00:01:27.662 --> 00:01:28.741
And we could craft. Like,

00:01:28.742 --> 00:01:30.781
if I wanted to build my own skill myself,

00:01:30.782 --> 00:01:32.481
I could literally just, like,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.580
you know, choose what type of skill it is,

00:01:34.581 --> 00:01:35.701
give it a name, description,

00:01:35.702 --> 00:01:37.461
and have it build that out for me.

00:01:37.462 --> 00:01:40.921
But the main system we have here is.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.540
This is clawhub, right?

00:01:42.541 --> 00:01:44.301
This essentially is a website

00:01:44.302 --> 00:01:45.641
you can go on

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:51.100
to download skills that are made by other people on Openclaw.

00:01:51.101 --> 00:01:53.201
So these are all different skills

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.220
that you can download for your AI agent

00:01:55.221 --> 00:01:57.221
that was made by somebody else.

00:01:57.222 --> 00:01:59.021
And the issue with this site here is

00:01:59.022 --> 00:02:00.941
you can't trust any of these skills,

00:02:00.942 --> 00:02:04.821
and you can't trust any of the people that uploaded these skills,

00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:06.301
because you might get hacked.

00:02:06.302 --> 00:02:10.601
There might be some malware in the skill files that you're downloading.

00:02:11.059 --> 00:02:13.860
And I found a way to combat this,

00:02:13.861 --> 00:02:16.001
in which I figured I would share with you guys,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.500
because I have my agent download these skills,

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.301
and you're probably like, oh,

00:02:21.302 --> 00:02:22.061
that's unsafe. No,

00:02:22.062 --> 00:02:24.361
it's not. I don't install the skill,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.520
I download it. I have the agent look through the internals of the skill,

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.660
and we simply replicate that skill

00:02:31.661 --> 00:02:36.361
rather than actually installing the skill made by whoever it is.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.940
So all the skills we have that my openclaw runs on

00:02:40.941 --> 00:02:43.741
is just replicated from other people on clawhub.

00:02:43.742 --> 00:02:44.501
And this isn't, like,

00:02:44.502 --> 00:02:46.581
bad or anything. All these skills are free.

00:02:46.582 --> 00:02:47.821
And you can't trust them anyway,

00:02:47.822 --> 00:02:50.581
so I would highly recommend,

00:02:50.582 --> 00:02:53.581
if you are to get any skills on clawhub,

00:02:53.582 --> 00:02:56.421
to just have your agent just replicate the skill

00:02:56.422 --> 00:02:58.181
rather than actually install it.

00:02:58.182 --> 00:03:01.341
Because I do not trust any of these people here,

00:03:01.342 --> 00:03:02.981
and I recommend you don't either.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.819
So I figured I'd give you guys some tips on that.
